  "prompt": "Design the CLIMATE INTELLIGENCE OVERVIEW DASHBOARD for ClimateGuard AI.\nPage Header: \"Climate Intelligence Overview\", Subtitle: \"Monitor environmental risks and disaster finance activity.\"\nTop Controls: Basin/Location selector (e.g. \"Global Overview - All Monitored Zones\"), Date range picker (\"Last 24 Hours • Live Telemetry\"), \"Refresh Stream\" action.\n\nROW 1 — 4 KPI CARDS:\n- Active Risk Zones: \"18 Active Basins\" (High Priority: 4, Moderate: 9, Low: 5), badge \"Live Satellite Telemetry\"\n- Flood Risk: \"Critical Warning (88%)\" - Rio Paraná Basin, peak discharge 14,200 m³/s, trend +18% vs 10yr baseline\n- Heatwave Risk: \"High Risk (76%)\" - Rajasthan Sector, max temp 46.2°C, WBGT 31.8°C\n- Drought Risk: \"Severe Deficit (64%)\" - Horn of Africa Zone 4, soil moisture -41% anomaly\n\nROW 2:\n- LEFT (2/3 width): Large Climate Risk Geospatial Map viewport with multi-hazard overlays, active warning hotspots with pulsing rings, coordinates display, satellite/topographic basemap toggle, and layer legend.\n- RIGHT (1/3 width): Risk Distribution breakdown chart with categorical hazard split (42% Flood, 31% Heatwave, 27% Drought) and risk level breakdown bars.\n\nROW 3:\n- LEFT: Multi-metric Weather Trends Chart (Interactive multi-series preview: Temperature °C, Rainfall mm, and Humidity % over past 48h with forecast projection).\n- RIGHT: Hazard Summary matrix cards detailing Flood (4 active alerts), Heatwave (6 active alerts), Drought (8 active alerts) with quick-drill triggers.\n\nROW 4:\n- Recent Incidents Table:\n  Columns: Incident ID, Location, Hazard Type, Risk Level (colored badges #EF4444, #F97316, etc.), Detected Date/Time, Status (Active / Under Review / Mitigated), View Action button.\n  5 realistic incidents with real geographic basins.\n\nROW 5:\n- Automated Funding Activity:\n  KPI mini-cards: Triggered Rules (7), Pending Requests ($4.2M), Approved Simulations ($18.5M), Recent Activity ledger. Include clear \"Parametric Simulation Mode\" badge.",
